cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "vissue: plain-text issue tracking in orgmode files"
message: "If you use vissue, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rohit
    family-names: Goswami
    email: rgoswami@ieee.org
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2393-8056"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HaoZeke/vissue"
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - issue tracking
  - orgmode
  - directed acyclic graph
  - multi-agent
  - plain text
  - command line
  - model context protocol
abstract: >-
  vissue tracks issues as top-level orgmode headings in one file per project.
  Parent and blocker edges form an explicit DAG: ready is the open frontier,
  claim is the multi-agent lock, and related ranks a named local neighborhood
  without writing inferred links. The file is the store, so the backlog diffs,
  merges, and greps alongside the code it describes. A CLI and a Model Context
  Protocol server share one library, providing queries over state, priority,
  the graph, a JSONL export, and a read-only projection for sharing a backlog
  with collaborators who cannot read the tracker directly.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "OokCite"
    notes: "Citation graph, PageRank prior, and neighbourhood ranking research that the vissue DAG follows."
